WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.660
Dragonriders, dreamers, and dragonknights.&nbsp;
The Targaryen dynasty ruled for centuries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:09.480
but who conquered, and who was deemed "unworthy"?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:14.134
We’re climbing the branches of one of&nbsp;
the messiest family trees in Westeros.

00:00:14.134 --> 00:00:19.200
During House of the Dragon, the Targaryens&nbsp;
rule Westeros. But they have more humble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.660
origins than their wealth and dragons suggest,&nbsp;
and aren't even from the western continent. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:29.580
family can trace its roots back to Valyria,&nbsp;
the one-time capital city of the Freehold in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:34.560
Essos. As King Viserys explains to Alicent&nbsp;
Hightower, Valyria was a city so great,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:40.500
the world hadn't seen its equal in the century&nbsp;
since its destruction. In The World of Ice &amp; Fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.580
George R. R. Martin points out how&nbsp;
the Targaryens were among dozens of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:48.840
dragon-riding families who called Valyria&nbsp;
home, but they weren't a major power.

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:54.600
While their mass exodus was seen as an act of&nbsp;
weakness, only three houses escaped Valyria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.600 --> 00:01:00.300
before it was destroyed: the Targaryens, the&nbsp;
Velaryons, and the Celtigars. They survived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.700
because of the visions of Daenys Targaryen — also&nbsp;
known as Daenys the Dreamer — which prophesied&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:10.920
the fiery downfall of their civilization.&nbsp;
Her father, Aenar, had uprooted his people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:16.980
and fled about 12 years before the Doom fell&nbsp;
on Valyria, which included Daenys' brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:23.760
Gaemon. Gaemon married Daenys and ruled as Lord of&nbsp;
Dragonstone after his father. For about 70 years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:28.680
Targaryens remained at Dragonstone and&nbsp;
continued wedding sisters to brothers.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.440
Aegon Targaryen is clearly the most important&nbsp;
figure in Martin's fantastical fictional history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:39.900
This second child of Lord Aerion Targaryen&nbsp;
would marry both his older sister, Visenya,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.940
and his younger sister, Rhaenys. Though it&nbsp;
is believed that Aegon married Visenya out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:51.420
of expectation and Rhaenys because he was smitten.&nbsp;
He first sired the child Aenys with Rhaenys. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:56.880
child with Visenya — named Maegor— came along&nbsp;
five years later. But before there was a crown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.640
and a throne for either of them to inherit, Aegon&nbsp;
had to earn his nickname and do some conquering.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:08.389
"Say what you will about the Targaryens, they&nbsp;
were conquerors. That is a seat for a conqueror."

00:02:08.389 --> 00:02:13.560
The full story of Aegon's conquest of the Seven&nbsp;
Kingdoms of Westeros could fill several seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:18.600
of another Game of Thrones prequel series. House&nbsp;
of the Dragon adds a motivation for Aegon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:24.000
conquest besides raw ambition: He had a dream&nbsp;
about a coming threat from the North which he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.660
etched into the blade of the catspaw&nbsp;
dagger he inherited from his ancestor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:32.100
Lord Aenar. Aegon believed that&nbsp;
only a Targaryen king or queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:36.906
with dragons was formidable enough&nbsp;
to face whatever danger was to come.

00:02:36.906 --> 00:02:42.000
There's bound to be tension in a love&nbsp;
triangle. It was no different with Aegon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:47.100
Visenya, Rhaenys, and their children. Since the&nbsp;
king preferred the company of his younger wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.220
he kept Rhaenys and Aenys&nbsp;
with him at King's Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:55.920
while Visenya and Maegor lived at Dragonstone.&nbsp;
The two princes had little in common and didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.320
care for each other. Aenys was undersized&nbsp;
and sickly, which spurred rumors that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:07.020
wasn't actually Aegon's son. But he grew up to&nbsp;
be a dreamer and a dragonrider like his father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:12.900
possessing gifts that Aegon did not. He was&nbsp;
charming, sociable, talented, and clever.

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:18.600
When Aegon died of a stroke around age 64,&nbsp;
Aenys hurried on his dragon Quicksilver to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:24.180
the funeral and was declared the next king. In a&nbsp;
political calculation, he bequeathed his father's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:30.120
ancestral sword, Blackfyre, to his half-brother&nbsp;
Maegor and suggested they'd rule together. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:34.980
knew Maegor — who was an enormous warrior&nbsp;
without an equal — would be a better ally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:39.600
than an enemy. The King's personal life was&nbsp;
fruitful, having six children with his wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:45.540
Alyssa Velaryon. But his reign was not. After five&nbsp;
years of rebellions and assassination attempts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:50.340
Aenys died — with some believing that&nbsp;
Visenya and Maegor orchestrated his death.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:55.800
Maegor was almost the inverse of his&nbsp;
half-brother, taking six wives but having&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.600
no surviving children. While he is responsible&nbsp;
for completing much of the construction of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:05.820
King's Landing, his burning of the Sept of&nbsp;
Remembrance, mass executions of builders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.820 --> 00:04:11.334
and general oppression of Westeros' people&nbsp;
earned him the nickname Maegor the Cruel.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:16.020
Maegor was found dead of mysterious&nbsp;
circumstances on the Iron Throne. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.580
had no heir, so the succession passed to&nbsp;
Aenys and Alyssa's oldest surviving son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:26.520
Jaehaerys. The Faith of the Seven — the dominant&nbsp;
religion in Westeros — had risen against Aenys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:31.200
when he betrothed his children, Rhaena and&nbsp;
Aegon, to each other. The siblings were later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:36.000
killed. Following in his family's tradition, the&nbsp;
new 14-year-old King Jaehaerys wanted to marry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.904
his sister Alysanne. His mother Alyssa tried&nbsp;
to forbid it, fearing a war with the church.

00:04:40.904 --> 00:04:44.880
"I serve the gods. The gods demand justice."

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.134
"How do they communicate their&nbsp;
demands? By raven or horse?"

00:04:49.134 --> 00:04:54.360
But the King would get his way, wedding Alysanne&nbsp;
in secret. When he instituted the "Doctrine of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:59.580
Exceptionalism" when he came of age, he ensured&nbsp;
that only Targaryen royals could enter into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.980
sibling marriages. He made peace with Maegor's few&nbsp;
remaining loyalists by restoring their titles and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:11.040
lands, so long as they recognized his legitimacy.&nbsp;
Jaehaerys and Alysanne were almost always together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:17.280
throughout his prosperous 45-year dynasty. Though&nbsp;
Jaehaerys was one of the Seven Kingdoms' most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:23.801
effective rulers, his long life and legendary&nbsp;
fertility created the conditions for civil war.

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:30.300
Of Jaehaerys and Alysanne's 13 children, only&nbsp;
one survived their father's reign. The king and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:37.680
queen's first, 11th, and 12th children died in&nbsp;
infancy, while their 2nd, 6th, 10th, and 13th met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:43.320
their ends in a variety of ways in their teenage&nbsp;
years. Their 8th child, Daella, reached adulthood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:49.200
but passed away during a difficult labor. Their&nbsp;
9th, Saera, was a troubled girl who ran away to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.600
Volantis where she operated a pleasure house and&nbsp;
bore many illegitimate children — she wasn't heard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:59.520
from again. As King Jaehaerys reached old&nbsp;
age, just 4 of his offspring remained alive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:07.440
and at court: his 3rd child, Aemon, his 4th,&nbsp;
Baelon, his 5th, Alyssa, and his 7th, Vaegon.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:12.660
Jaehaerys named Aemon his heir and Prince&nbsp;
of Dragonstone. Baelon and Alyssa married&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:18.540
each other. Vaegon became an archmaester. The&nbsp;
succession seemed secure until Aemon was killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:23.580
in battle during a conflict in Myr. He left behind&nbsp;
a wife, Lady Jocelyn Baratheon, and a daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:29.160
Rhaenys Targaryen — who had recently married&nbsp;
Corlys Velaryon. Baelon was made the new Prince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:34.020
of Dragonstone. His sister-wife, Princess Alyssa,&nbsp;
had perished giving birth to their third child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:39.000
after their sons Viserys and Daemon were born,&nbsp;
leaving Jaehaerys and Alysanne with two surviving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:44.100
heirs. Then Baelon succumbed to appendicitis&nbsp;
just five days later. House of the Dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:48.840
insinuates that Otto Hightower may have plotted&nbsp;
the Prince's death to advance his own position,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:54.660
but in the end, Vaegon was the single&nbsp;
Targaryen child to outlive King Jaehaerys.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:07:00.480
Baelon's death caused a Westerosi crisis. The&nbsp;
King's advisors and the Lords of the Realm all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:06.120
agreed that Vaegon wasn't a viable candidate for&nbsp;
the crown, as he was unpopular and disinterested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:11.820
in leadership. Only two were considered&nbsp;
reasonable: Aemon's grandson Laenor Velaryon, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:18.060
Baelon aand Alyssa's son Viserys. King Jaehaerys&nbsp;
convened what's known as the Great Council of 101&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:24.420
AC at Harrenhal, where a thousand lords took six&nbsp;
months to gather and decide who should succeed the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:29.400
long-reigning king. Though Aemon was the older&nbsp;
prince and Rhaenys thought his line should have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:34.980
the stronger claim, the lords chose Viserys as&nbsp;
he was 24 years in age, compared to Laenor's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:39.780
7 years — though in House of the Dragon, they&nbsp;
choose Viserys over Rhaenys because he is male.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:46.560
"Men would sooner put the realm to the torch,&nbsp;
than see a woman ascend the Iron Throne."

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.240
But the Council's vote didn't resolve the&nbsp;
succession with as much finality that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:55.980
King had hoped for. Viserys ascended the Iron&nbsp;
Throne two years later when Jaehaerys died in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.980 --> 00:08:00.720
his sleep. Around the time Viserys' wife Aemma&nbsp;
died in childbirth. As a result, he named his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:06.540
daughter Rhaenyra as his heir and Princess of&nbsp;
Dragonstone. This angered his brother Daemon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:11.520
who coveted the title and assumed he'd follow&nbsp;
his brother as the next Targaryen king. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:16.380
he remained supportive of Rhaenyra's claim to&nbsp;
the Iron Throne, Viserys took a second wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:23.040
Alicent Hightower, with whom he had four more&nbsp;
children: Aegon, Helaena, Aemond, and Daeron.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:28.980
King Viserys insisted Rhaenyra marry Laenor&nbsp;
Velaryon. Though their union was a political&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:34.380
arrangement — with Laenor preferring the company&nbsp;
of men — they produced three children: Jacaerys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:39.960
Lucerys, and Joffrey Velaryon. In truth,&nbsp;
however, these boys were likely the sons of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:45.720
Ser Harwin Strong, Rhaenyra's rumored lover and&nbsp;
Captain of the Gold Cloaks. All three resembled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:51.600
the man known as Breakbones with their bulky&nbsp;
physiques, broad noses, and brown hair. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:56.580
complicated Rhaenyra's legitimacy in the eyes&nbsp;
of some at court and among some common folk.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:01.800
They believed that if her sons were illegitimate,&nbsp;
they had no business sitting on the Iron Throne.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:07.380
Though Rhaenyra and Daemon were rivals on paper,&nbsp;
they always enjoyed a close relationship. Around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:11.880
the same time she wed Laenor, Daemon — free&nbsp;
to marry again after the death of his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.740
wife — married Laenor's sister Laena. The&nbsp;
happy dragon-riding couple had twin daughters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:22.380
Baela and Rhaena, before Laena died laboring&nbsp;
with their stillborn son. Shortly thereafter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.380 --> 00:09:25.500
Laenor was allegedly killed&nbsp;
in a fight with his companion.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:30.480
Before the customary mourning period was&nbsp;
over, Rhaenyra and Daemon exchanged vows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:34.500
without King Viserys' permission. They&nbsp;
would have two fully Targaryen sons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.500 --> 00:09:40.500
Aegon and Viserys. Since Rhaenyra's claim&nbsp;
was tenuous despite her father's decree and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:45.180
the lords' oaths, so was the position&nbsp;
of her five sons. Those who supported&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:48.720
her line were called the Blacks.&nbsp;
In the books, this is a reference&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:53.601
to a dress the Princess wore at her father&nbsp;
and Alicent's fifth anniversary celebration.

00:09:53.601 --> 00:09:59.400
The rivals of the Blacks were the Greens —&nbsp;
so named for Queen Alicent's green gown. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:04.740
Greens backed Viserys and Alicent's firstborn&nbsp;
son, though Aegon's only claim was that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:09.540
was male and Rhaenyra was not. Thanks to&nbsp;
his grandfather and mother's statecraft,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:14.700
the Greens were able to win young Aegon many&nbsp;
allies. Alicent married her son to his sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:20.220
Halaena, and the teenage bride quickly became&nbsp;
pregnant with twins, whom she named Jaehaerys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:24.540
and Jaehaera. While the couple would later&nbsp;
welcome another son — Maelor— Aegon was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:30.000
thought to have depraved sexual appetites and&nbsp;
possibly sired many more illegitimate children.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.400
"Think of the shame on your&nbsp;
wife. On me. How can you keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:38.280
carrying on like this?&nbsp;
Especially on a day like today."

00:10:39.000 --> 00:10:43.200
Because the Greens remained at King's Landing&nbsp;
while the Blacks were often found at Dragonstone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.920
Alicent and Aegon were privy to the&nbsp;
news of the death of King Viserys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:51.900
first. Aegon II was installed as the new&nbsp;
king before word reached Princess Rhaenyra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:56.880
who crowned herself in a separate ceremony in&nbsp;
response to her half-brother's treason. Aegon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.880 --> 00:11:02.340
II would rule over a kingdom in a civil&nbsp;
war for about two years. The scheming and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:06.600
dragon battles between the Greens and the&nbsp;
Blacks resulted in the deaths of Aegon's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:12.060
sister-wife Halaena and his three sons.&nbsp;
With his defeat seeming imminent, Aegon II&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:17.668
was poisoned by a group of conspirators at his&nbsp;
court, likely to prevent any further cruelty.

00:11:17.668 --> 00:11:22.980
Peace finally returned to the realm with the&nbsp;
ascension of King Aegon III. While Rhaenyra and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:29.040
Daemon both died during the Dance of Dragons — as&nbsp;
did her sons Jacaerys, Lucerys, and Joffrey — her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.740
children with Daemon, Aegon and Viserys, survived.&nbsp;
Jaehaera, the daughter of Aegon II and Halaena,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:40.140
also survived. While these cousins were sworn&nbsp;
enemies, they eventually married each other. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.060
five years, Aegon III was too young to rule and&nbsp;
a group of regents worked to mend the kingdom's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.060 --> 00:11:49.620
divisions. However, the king could not be mended&nbsp;
after the trauma he'd witnessed and experienced,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:54.720
becoming known as Aegon the Unlucky,&nbsp;
Aegon the Unhappy, and Aegon the Broken.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:59.040
Jaehaera suffered invisible wounds&nbsp;
from the Dance as well. She threw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:03.720
herself from a window before she and her&nbsp;
cousin-husband could consummate the match,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:09.960
thus ending the genetic line of the Greens. Aegon&nbsp;
III took Daenaera Velaryon as his second wife,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:17.640
and she gave him five children. After a 25-year&nbsp;
reign, Aegon III died of consumption at only 36&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:23.820
years old. His sons, Daeron and Baelor, became the&nbsp;
next two Targaryen kings, but both of their stints&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.820 --> 00:12:29.040
on the throne were cut short by their own fatal&nbsp;
flaws. Daeron was killed trying to conquer Dorne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:34.440
before he could produce heirs. Baelor was a&nbsp;
religious fanatic who remained celebate even after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:39.577
he was married to his sister, Daena. He eventually&nbsp;
died because of a self-imposed hunger strike.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:45.840
Daemon and Rhaenyra's second son, Viserys, had&nbsp;
been Hand to the last three monarchs, so he was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:51.720
well-prepared for the job when he became the 10th&nbsp;
Targaryen King. King Viserys II was more like his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.720 --> 00:12:57.300
great-great-grandfather, Jaehaerys, rather than&nbsp;
his namesake. He was an excellent communicator and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.300 --> 00:13:03.420
reformer that improved life throughout Westeros.&nbsp;
He established a central bank, expanded freedoms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:09.240
and improved trade relations, all within his&nbsp;
first year on the Iron Throne. Unfortunately, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:15.240
was his only year on the throne: Viserys II died&nbsp;
unexpectedly at age 50 due to a sudden illness.

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:21.660
"The sickness struck him&nbsp;
very hard. And very fast. "

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:27.720
Rhaenyra and Daemon's last child continued their&nbsp;
line with Targaryen children of his own — Aemon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:34.020
Aegon, and Naerys — born of his wife Larra Rogare.&nbsp;
Aemon became a member of the Kingsguard and went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:39.540
down in history as the legendary Dragonknight.&nbsp;
King Aegon IV succeeded his father as king,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:45.480
married his sister Naerys, and cemented his&nbsp;
legacy as Aegon the Unworthy — a corrupt and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:51.600
hedonistic monarch, surrounded with yes men and&nbsp;
mistresses, who plunged the kingdoms into ruin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:58.440
His uncontrollable lust led him to father at least&nbsp;
13 illegitimate children, while only producing two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:04.920
trueborn children with Queen Naerys — Daeron and&nbsp;
Daenerys. Worst of all, Aegon IV is suspected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:10.260
of having poisoned his own father, Viserys&nbsp;
II, to hasten his ascension to the throne.

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:16.260
Aegon the Unworthy caused chaos even after&nbsp;
his disastrous reign. Before he died from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:21.540
his own sloth and gluttony, he legitimized his&nbsp;
bastards and bequeathed the ancestral sword&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:28.800
Blackfyre to his eldest, Daemon Waters. Aegon&nbsp;
IV resented his trueborn son Daeron and began&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:33.300
a rumor that the prince was really the love&nbsp;
child of his brother, Aemon the Dragonknight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:37.800
and his sister-wife Naerys, in an attempt&nbsp;
to undermine Daemon's succession claim.

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:43.560
Daemon renamed himself Daemon Blackfyre and&nbsp;
gathered an army to oppose the new King Daeron II.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:49.800
Thus, the Targaryens and the Kingdoms were torn&nbsp;
apart by a second and longer civil war. Daeron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:55.320
was popular with some Westerosi lords because&nbsp;
he was everything his father was not — cultured,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:55.320 --> 00:15:00.540
diplomatic, just — and he had finally united&nbsp;
Dorne with the rest of Westeros through his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:05.520
marriage to Myriah Martell. Others sided with&nbsp;
Daemon Blackfyre, as there was still animosity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:10.500
toward Dorne after so many losses there. They&nbsp;
thought Daemon's possession of Blackfyre, his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:15.000
father's final decree, and his military&nbsp;
prowess made him the stronger claimant.

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:19.380
In total, there would be five Blackfyre&nbsp;
Rebellions over the course of half a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.380 --> 00:15:25.800
century. Daeron II was succeeded by his son&nbsp;
Aerys I, who had no heirs, and Maekar I — who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:32.701
had six children with his wife Dyanna Dayne:&nbsp;
Daeron, Aerion, Aemon, Daella, Aegon, and Rhae.

00:15:32.701 --> 00:15:36.180
The story of Maekar's children&nbsp;
is told in Martin's anthology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:41.460
A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms. Maekar's&nbsp;
eldest son, Daeron the Dreamer — or Daeron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:46.860
the Drunk — was tormented by prophetic visions&nbsp;
and died of pox. His second son, Aerion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:52.740
believed himself to be a dragon in human form,&nbsp;
and accidentally took his own life by drinking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:59.400
wildfire — hoping it would reveal his "true" form.&nbsp;
This left Maekar's third son, Aemon, next in line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:03.600
except he had become a maester. Another Great&nbsp;
Council was convened with the questions:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:09.180
Should Aemon be released from his vows?&nbsp;
Or should Aegon — Maekar's fourth son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:13.445
who had been living as a peasant with the&nbsp;
knight Ser Duncan — be crowned instead?

00:16:13.980 --> 00:16:17.640
"The gods were cruel when&nbsp;
they saw fit to test my vows."

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:23.520
They shouldn't have bothered, as Aemon abdicated&nbsp;
the Iron Throne and banished himself to the Wall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:29.220
so that he couldn't be used against his brother.&nbsp;
King Aegon V became the 15th Targaryen king,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.220 --> 00:16:33.240
reigning for nearly 25 years over a&nbsp;
kingdom that was intermittently at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:37.800
war with the Blackfyres. He'd married Betha&nbsp;
Blackwood of his own accord years earlier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:44.280
and they had five children: Duncan, Jaehaerys,&nbsp;
Shaera, Daeron, and Rhaelle. This king and queen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:50.100
wanted to move away from the Targaryen tradition&nbsp;
of incestual marriage, and arranged marriages for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.100 --> 00:16:54.600
their children with the other great Westerosi&nbsp;
houses, like the Baratheons and the Tullys.

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:58.800
Duncan renounced the throne to marry&nbsp;
a peasant named Jenny of Oldstones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:03.420
while Jaehaerys and Shaera married each&nbsp;
other. King Jaehaerys II would succeed his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:08.820
father after the Tragedy at Summerhall in which&nbsp;
Aegon V, Duncan, and many others were killed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:14.013
This reportedly occurred when the king tried to&nbsp;
hatch dragon eggs, setting the palace on fire.

00:17:14.378 --> 00:17:19.620
Jaehaerys II and Shaera had two children of&nbsp;
their own: Aerys and Rhaella. Though they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:22.980
had wed for passion, they joined their&nbsp;
son and daughter together against King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:28.140
Aegon V's wishes due to a witch's prophecy.&nbsp;
The witch predicted that the fabled Prince&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:33.540
Who Was Promised would come from their union.&nbsp;
Knowing what we now know about Aegon I's dream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:38.040
this was likely a stronger motivating&nbsp;
factor for Jaehaerys, rather than tradition.

00:17:38.040 --> 00:17:43.800
Jaehaerys II died of illness, and Aerys II&nbsp;
ascended to the throne. He and his sister-wife&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:50.460
Rhaelle had three children — Rhaegar, Viserys,&nbsp;
and Daenerys— but lost many more to miscarriage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:56.160
and stillbirth. Aerys had dallied with mistresses&nbsp;
early on, but he came to believe the deaths of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:56.160 --> 00:18:01.680
his children were punishment for his infidelity.&nbsp;
When Rhaegar survived, he swore faithfulness to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:07.080
his wife. However, he became superstitious, then&nbsp;
outright paranoid. He blamed failed pregnancies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:12.540
on his wife Rhaella's supposed cheating,&nbsp;
imprisoning her under guard in Maegor's Holdfast.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:19.140
As the Mad King grew vengeful and unhinged, the&nbsp;
Targaryen dynasty fell apart. Growing suspicious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:23.460
that his one-time friend and Hand, Tywin&nbsp;
Lannister, was conspiring to overthrow him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:28.200
he married his eldest son Rhaegar to Elia&nbsp;
Martell of Dorne. The Mad King also became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:33.720
obsessed with wildfire, using it to execute&nbsp;
his perceived enemies. He intended to blow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:39.120
up the city should Robert Baratheon's rebellion&nbsp;
prevail. Instead, his Kingsguard Jamie Lannister&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.120 --> 00:18:43.234
assassinated him before the message to&nbsp;
carry out the order could be delivered.

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:49.200
During the rebellion, the Mad King had his son&nbsp;
Viserys, and wife Rhaella — who was then pregnant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:49.200 --> 00:18:54.180
with Daenerys — ferried away to Dragonstone. He&nbsp;
kept Rhaegar's family with him at the Red Keep,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:57.780
where they were all brutally killed&nbsp;
during the Sack of King's Landing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.780 --> 00:19:03.180
along with Rhaegar himself. While Robert claimed&nbsp;
Rhaegar kidnapped and violated his betrothed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:07.020
Lyanna Stark, Game of Thrones&nbsp;
reveals they had actually married,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.020 --> 00:19:11.700
and that their baby — Aegon Targaryen — was&nbsp;
born out of love. Lyanna made her brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:18.000
Ned promise to keep this secret, and the&nbsp;
child was concealed under the name Jon Snow.

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:24.660
"You've never been a bastard. You are Aegon&nbsp;
Targaryen, true heir to the Iron Throne."

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:30.300
Robert became king and married Cersei Lannister.&nbsp;
Like Rhaenyra before her, Cersei had three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:34.860
illegitimate children with her brother Jaime,&nbsp;
but none lived long enough to produce any heirs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:40.740
and the Lannister family line died out. Elsewhere,&nbsp;
Viserys and Daenerys Targaryen lived in exile in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:45.540
the free cities. Daenerys expected to wed her&nbsp;
brother to strengthen the family line, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:51.360
Viserys married her to Khal Drogo of the Dothraki&nbsp;
to secure a large enough army to retake the Iron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:57.720
Throne. When Viserys offended the new Khaleesi and&nbsp;
her people, they poured molten gold over his head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:57.720 --> 00:20:03.300
killing him. Daenerys would give birth to a&nbsp;
stillborn son, and though she consummated her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:08.460
relationship with her nephew, Jon Snow, he was&nbsp;
forced to slay her after she laid waste to King's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:14.918
Landing. This left Jon — or Aegon — the last&nbsp;
hanging leaf on the Targaryen family tree.

